# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/ship-4 window (the combined ship candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/ship-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-ship-4/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C1 (TIMED, the CONTROL of the first decode ABAB pair): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic, the approved fusion ship profile as production would run
# it after the fusion cutover (two M3 blocks, W2, engine reuse, every fusion lever, no octo, no oneq, no grid13, no tier), eight live (concurrent8_steady), eight at 32k and
# 120k with 800-token answers (concurrent8_code_32k / _128k) and eight at depth for the whole all-live window (concurrent8_code_32k_long, concurrent8_code_128k_long). Every
# boot a fresh reset. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. The two _long tests are the
# DEEP tests: eight real-code prompts of about 32k / 120k tokens with budgets (3,000 / 4,000, ignore_eos) that outlast the prefill queue, so that the last user arrives
# while the first is still decoding and eight seats decode together at depth; the 800-token concurrent8_code_32k / _128k (run beside them for continuity) never have six
# seats live at once, so no octo round runs in them. READ: c2_smoke_check clean, no stall; this log is the reference of L1 (octo_compare.py --control <this smoke log>
# --octo <L1 smoke log>: every answer equal, user by user) and of the floor (C1 against C2). TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC
# sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step; read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first [TELEMETRY] line must say
# decode check ok. A gain that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): 65 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k,concurrent8_code_32k_long,concurrent8_code_128k_long
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=100
